WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.546 --> 00:00:16.186
turned to Flo.

2
00:00:16.206 --> 00:00:18.607
"What's a VIP?"

3
00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:20.068
she asked nervously.

4
00:00:20.088 --> 00:00:24.850
"It stands for Very Important Person," Flo said.

5
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:30.032
"Oh!" Ally sighed in relief.

6
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.801
"In this case, it refers to the president of the National League of Rocket Scientists," Ray said.

7
00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:40.223
"The local league has been trying to get him to come to their gala for years, but he

8
00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:41.203
always turns them down.

9
00:00:42.003 --> 00:00:45.344
But when he heard it was going to be here at the diner, he changed his mind."

10
00:00:45.364 --> 00:00:50.246
"That's a big compliment to you, Ray," Flo said.

11
00:00:50.266 --> 00:00:51.806
"You think so?"

12
00:00:52.346 --> 00:00:52.946
Ray asked.

13
00:00:53.827 --> 00:00:54.447
Flo nodded.

14
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:58.288
"Your reputation is what's bringing him here."

15
00:00:59.596 --> 00:01:03.899
"But still, I think I should add some fancier dishes to the menu," Ray said.

16
00:01:03.919 --> 00:01:08.562
"I'd be happy to help you come up with some ideas," Flo said.

17
00:01:09.563 --> 00:01:10.603
Ray looked relieved.

18
00:01:10.623 --> 00:01:11.944
"Thanks, Flo.

19
00:01:12.745 --> 00:01:14.266
Well, I'd better get back to work."

20
00:01:16.147 --> 00:01:17.968
Ally and Flo returned to the dining room.

21
00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:23.452
"We should come up with an extra special dessert," Flo said.

22
00:01:23.472 --> 00:01:27.394
"Something to really impress the president."

23
00:01:28.175 --> 00:01:29.476
Randy stepped out of the kitchen.

24
00:01:30.352 --> 00:01:31.933
"I can bake a special cake.

25
00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:35.336
I've entered a few baking contests in my day."

26
00:01:35.356 --> 00:01:37.598
"You have?"

27
00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:38.639
Flo said.

28
00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:41.201
"I had no idea."

29
00:01:42.682 --> 00:01:46.285
Randy pulled out his phone and showed Ally and Flo photos of some of his cakes.

30
00:01:47.086 --> 00:01:51.069
There was a cake that looked like a turkey dinner, one that looked like a box of cereal,

31
00:01:51.589 --> 00:01:53.491
and even one that looked like a cell phone.

32
00:01:53.511 --> 00:01:56.974
"These are amazing!"

33
00:01:57.414 --> 00:01:59.496
Ally exclaimed as she scrolled through the pictures.

34
00:02:00.708 --> 00:02:04.791
"I was thinking I could make a rocket ship cake for the gala," Randy said.

35
00:02:04.811 --> 00:02:07.033
"That would be perfect!"

36
00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:08.014
Flo said.

37
00:02:11.396 --> 00:02:14.118
Later Mateo came to plan the scavenger hunt with Ally.

38
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.923
"The one my parents planned for me was cool," Ally said.

39
00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:26.468
"They hid clues everywhere—all over our ship, outside, and at a playground.

40
00:02:26.828 --> 00:02:30.969
The final prize was a day on the moon of Formaria for me and my friends.

41
00:02:31.749 --> 00:02:36.411
Formaria has just enough gravity to make it like a giant bouncy house.

42
00:02:38.011 --> 00:02:39.752
It was so much fun."

43
00:02:39.772 --> 00:02:45.693
"I wish I could take Bethany to Formaria," Mateo said.

44
00:02:45.713 --> 00:02:48.314
"Me too," Ally said.

45
00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.335
"What will you make the big final prize?"

46
00:02:51.355 --> 00:02:57.036
"A T-shirt from our favorite show, Cosmic Quest," Mateo said.

47
00:02:57.056 --> 00:03:01.558
"I'm going to make all the gifts fit the theme of the show.

48
00:03:02.179 --> 00:03:06.240
And I can plant the clues here at the diner, the park, oh, and at one of the

49
00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.261
artist's sculptures.

50
00:03:08.141 --> 00:03:11.242
Now we just need to write some fun riddles for Bethany to solve."

51
00:03:11.262 --> 00:03:13.383
"Fun riddles?"

52
00:03:13.803 --> 00:03:14.283
Ally said.

53
00:03:14.303 --> 00:03:16.084
"I already have one!

54
00:03:17.085 --> 00:03:20.486
What's hotter than the moon but colder than Jupiter in winter?"

55
00:03:22.047 --> 00:03:22.927
Mateo shrugged.

56
00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:24.968
"I have no idea."

57
00:03:26.532 --> 00:03:28.673
"A galactic freezer!"

58
00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:32.875
Ally laughed.

59
00:03:32.915 --> 00:03:35.676
But to her surprise Mateo just looked confused.

60
00:03:35.696 --> 00:03:38.617
"Hmm," he said politely.

61
00:03:38.637 --> 00:03:42.199
"I'm not sure that riddle will work here on Earth.

62
00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:49.302
How about this one: Give me a tap and I'll give you some suds, I come in handy

63
00:03:49.622 --> 00:03:50.923
when you're covered in mud."

64
00:03:52.423 --> 00:03:53.524
Ally scratched her head.

65
00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:56.522
"A solar bath?"

66
00:03:56.542 --> 00:03:59.105
"No, silly."

67
00:04:00.867 --> 00:04:01.808
Mateo laughed.

68
00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:07.575
"Soap!" "I would never have guessed that."

69
00:04:08.075 --> 00:04:08.696
Ally grinned.

70
00:04:08.716 --> 00:04:13.081
"We can leave that clue on the soap dispenser in the ladies' restroom here."

71
00:04:13.101 --> 00:04:15.284
"Fantastic idea!"

72
00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:25.757
That evening Ray cooked a special dinner to welcome Ally to the house.

73
00:04:31.119 --> 00:04:32.879
famous enchiladas, just for you, Ally!"

74
00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:33.739
Ray said.

75
00:04:33.759 --> 00:04:36.560
"These look delicious, Ray.

76
00:04:37.301 --> 00:04:41.262
Thank you so much for letting me stay with you," Ally said.

77
00:04:42.182 --> 00:04:42.942
Ray smiled.

78
00:04:42.962 --> 00:04:48.284
"Like I told Mateo, I'd do anything for—" Just then Alpha squawked loudly.

79
00:04:48.756 --> 00:04:52.557
"The weather on Saturn is 280 degrees with fog and rain."

80
00:04:53.898 --> 00:04:56.858
Ally blushed as she pulled the device out of her pocket and sat on it.

81
00:04:56.878 --> 00:04:58.919
"Sorry about that!

82
00:04:59.419 --> 00:05:01.240
This silly device is acting up."

83
00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.181
"No problem," Ray said.

84
00:05:04.201 --> 00:05:10.742
"As I was saying, I'd do—" The device started playing loud music before quickly switching to an annoying

85
00:05:10.802 --> 00:05:11.483
beeping sound.

86
00:05:12.383 --> 00:05:15.884
While Ally was trying to get Alpha to be quiet, she saw Ray frown.

87
00:05:17.516 --> 00:05:19.177
"I'm so sorry, Ray!"

88
00:05:19.598 --> 00:05:20.098
Ally said.

89
00:05:20.118 --> 00:05:22.080
"I'll go put this thing away."

90
00:05:26.063 --> 00:05:27.004
She hurried upstairs.

91
00:05:27.024 --> 00:05:31.007
"You're still not working right, Alpha," she whispered.

92
00:05:31.027 --> 00:05:33.389
"I'd better put you back on the charger."

93
00:05:35.611 --> 00:05:39.394
As Ally stepped back into the dining room, she heard Ray talking to Mateo.

94
00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:43.437
"This house is usually so quiet, and now it's filled with noise."

95
00:05:44.378 --> 00:05:45.258
Ray shook his head.

96
00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:46.840
"What a change."

97
00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:48.660
"Oh no!"

98
00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.921
Ally thought, her heart skipping a beat.

99
00:05:50.941 --> 00:05:55.663
"An Astralian has the duty to always be a good and peaceful guest.

100
00:05:56.324 --> 00:05:58.244
Alpha and I are breaking that rule!"
